# Course Recommendation System (DSA Project)

A content-based course recommendation engine that suggests courses to learners
based on their interests, skill level, and completed courses. Built to showcase
core Data Structures & Algorithms concepts.

## Problem Statement

Learners on online platforms are overwhelmed by thousands of courses and often
pick the wrong next step. This project recommends relevant courses by combining
text similarity (TF-IDF + cosine similarity) with a graph model of course
prerequisites, so recommendations respect both interest and learning order.

## Features

- Content-based recommendations using TF-IDF and cosine similarity
- k-Nearest Neighbors over course feature vectors
- Graph-based "next course" suggestions via BFS over prerequisites
- Filtering by difficulty and skill level
- REST API to serve recommendations
- Simple web frontend to query and display results

## Tech Stack

- Python 3.10+
- pandas, numpy, scikit-learn
- FastAPI + uvicorn (backend)
- HTML / CSS / JavaScript (frontend)

## Project Structure

```
course-recommender-dsa/
├── data/          # datasets (courses, users)
├── notebooks/     # exploratory analysis
├── src/           # core logic (preprocessing, recommender)
├── backend/       # FastAPI application
├── frontend/      # web UI
├── tests/         # unit tests
└── models/        # saved model artifacts
```

## Getting Started

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
python backend/app.py
```

## DSA Concepts Used

- Cosine similarity over sparse vectors
- k-NN search
- Graph traversal (BFS) for prerequisite chains
- Time/space complexity analysis of each recommender

